# WAZI Civic — Environment Configuration

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED for the live voice session
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your Google Gemini API key. This is read ONLY by the node proxy (server.js)
# and is never sent to the browser.
#
# Do NOT name this VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY. Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed
# variable into the client bundle, which publishes the key to anyone who opens
# devtools. The server still accepts the old name for backwards compatibility,
# but it warns loudly when it has to.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pin a specific Live model. It is moved to the front of the fallback chain
# rather than replacing it, so a bad value degrades instead of breaking voice.
# Verified working: gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview (default, fastest),
#                  gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-latest (more expressive, slower)
# GEMINI_LIVE_MODEL=

# Model used for photo/signboard clue extraction.
# GEMINI_VISION_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Country pack in use, injected into WAZI's civic context.
# WAZI_JURISDICTION=Nigeria

# Port for the proxy (the UI is served from here in production).
# PORT=8080

# Point the browser at a proxy on a different host. Normally unset: the client
# derives the socket URL from the page's own origin, which is what lets the dev
# server work from a phone on the same network.
# VITE_WS_PROXY_URL=

# Where `npm run dev` forwards /live and /api during development.
# WAZI_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8080

# Set to "quiet" to silence per-session proxy logging.
# WAZI_LOG=
